.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt TASKWARRIOR-SQUIRE 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm taskwarrior-squire
.Nd taskwarrior for one human and the AI assistants who work for them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm squire Cm init
.Pp
.Ev TASKRC Ns = Ns Pa $PREFIX/share/taskwarrior-squire/taskrc
.Ev TASKDATA Ns = Ns Pa <project>
.Ev SQUIRE_AUTHOR Ns = Ns Ar name
.Nm task Ar ...
.Pp
.Nm task Cm mine Op Ar filter
.Nm task Op Ar filter Cm board
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a taskwarrior configuration and one hook.
It adds a flow, an author, and length limits.
Every command is a
.Xr task 1
command.
.Ss Setup
.Nm squire Cm init
in the project root sets
.Ev TASKRC
to the installed taskrc and
.Ev TASKDATA
to the project, and prints both.
Set them for the project directory with any tool that sets a per-directory
environment, for example mise or direnv.
When
.Pa .claude/
exists, it also writes them with
.Ev SQUIRE_AUTHOR Ns =claude
into
.Pa .claude/settings.json
and writes into
.Pa .claude/skills/taskwarrior-squire/
a skill that reads the installed
.Pa SKILL.md ,
so an upgrade reaches the assistant.
The taskrc includes
.Pa ~/.taskrc
first, so your own settings apply.
.Pp
.Ev TASKDATA
is the directory that holds
.Pa taskchampion.sqlite3 .
If it sits in a git-tracked directory, you choose whether to commit it or to
ignore it.
It is a binary file: git shows no diff for it.
An assistant sets
.Ev SQUIRE_AUTHOR
to its own name.
Without it, the author is
.Ev USER .
.Ss Fields
.Bl -tag -width changed_by
.It Cm state
idea, open, doing, fixed, done, postponed or rejected.
A new task is an idea.
Done (verified) and rejected (won't fix, cannot reproduce, not needed)
close the task.
.Cm task Ar uuid Cm done
sets done, and
.Cm task Ar uuid Cm delete
sets rejected.
Another state opens the task again.
Comment why first.
.It Cm assignee
who acts next: the human for a question, an approval or a manual step.
.It Cm body
the details, line breaks allowed.
.It Cm version
the release the task belongs to.
.It Cm ref
the id the task had in another tracker.
.It Cm author , Cm changed_by
written by the hook.
.El
.Ss Rules
The hook refuses a change that breaks a rule.
.Bl -bullet
.It
A title is at most 80 characters, a body 800, a comment 500.
The limits bind everyone.
.It
Each new comment gets the prefix
.Li [author] .
.It
Only the human moves a task out of idea.
An assistant adds an idea, or a task tagged
.Cm +bug
in state open.
.It
An assistant moves a task only along the flow:
open to doing, doing to fixed, fixed to done.
It may send a task back to open, postpone it, or reject it.
The human moves a task to any state.
.El
.Ss Commands
.Bl -tag -width board
.It Cm mine
the live, unblocked tasks assigned to
.Ev SQUIRE_AUTHOR ,
most urgent first.
Each one shows what the assignee is asked:
the newest comment by someone else, else the body.
.It Cm board
every live task on one line: UUID, state, assignee, priority, version, ref
and title, most urgent first.
.El
.Pp
Refer to a task by its UUID prefix.
taskwarrior renumbers its short numeric ids.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $PREFIX/share/taskwarrior-squire/SKILL.md
how an assistant works with the human through these tasks
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
SQUIRE_AUTHOR=claude task add "Add rubocop to the demos" assignee:pirj
task 469e1a60 modify state:open assignee:claude
SQUIRE_AUTHOR=claude task 469e1a60 annotate "Which cops?"
task mine
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr task 1 ,
.Xr taskrc 5
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/pirj/taskwarrior-squire
